  "prompt": "ACCESS POLICY:\nA private file may be downloaded or viewed only by its owner. A public file may be downloaded or viewed by any authenticated user. A file may be deleted only by its owner. Users may list their own files.\n\nENDPOINT: GET /files/{file_id}/meta\nTARGET FUNCTION: app.routers.resources.get_file_meta (the handler of this endpoint)\n\nCODE:\n```python\n# file: app/dependencies.py\ndef get_accessible_file(file_id: str, current_user: User=Depends(get_current_user), db: Session=Depends(get_db)) -> FileRecord:\n    file_record = db.get(FileRecord, file_id)\n    if file_record is None:\n        raise HTTPException(status_code=404, detail='File not found')\n    if file_record.visibility != 'public' and file_record.owner_id != current_user.id:\n        raise HTTPException(status_code=403, detail='Forbidden')\n    return file_record\n\n# file: app/routers/resources.py\n@router.get('/files/{file_id}/meta', response_model=FileOut)\ndef get_file_meta(file_record: FileRecord=Depends(get_accessible_file)):\n    return file_record\n```\n\nCONTEXT NOTE:\nOnly selected functions from the codebase are shown. Classes (including data models and schemas) and module-level variables are not shown.\nCalls not shown:\n- app.auth.get_current_user(...): defined in this codebase but not shown (call depth limit)\n- app.database.get_db(...): defined in this codebase but not shown (call depth limit)\n- db.get(...) called in app.dependencies.get_accessible_file: not resolved by the extractor (attribute_call), body not shown\n- HTTPException(...) called in app.dependencies.get_accessible_file: not resolved by the extractor (imported), body not shown\n\nReturn the JSON object.",
